WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.210
- Hi, everybody!

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.043
It's Monday!

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.373
(audience applauding)
- Drew!

00:00:05.373 --> 00:00:08.180
- Gosh, I love Mondays!

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.850
Hi, everybody, welcome to the show.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.810
There is so much to talk about today.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.390
There are so many stories to cover.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.167
You know, Andy Cohen actually said to me,

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.290
"You are a walking mood board,"

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.750
and to that, I said, "Yeah, accurate."

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.580
And when I thought about the
show we were gonna make today,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.900
it felt like a mood board.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.690
We wanna talk about Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.230
We have Ross Matthews here to
discuss last night's Emmys.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.440
We have Jose Andres here to speak

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.400
about the life-changing
good that can be done

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.080
in the world of food.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.650
We have Paris Hilton,

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.770
who is in a different place in her life,

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.570
and she's opening up
to us about all of it,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.500
and I am truly able to connect with her

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.350
about something very
unique that we both share.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.350
So, hello, VFFs. Hi to you at home.

00:01:01.447 --> 00:01:03.441
(audience applauding)
Thanks for being with us.

00:01:03.441 --> 00:01:05.720
We're gonna get right into our news,

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.710
and we're gonna do it in our style,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.810
serving it sunny side up.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.327
It's time for "Drew's News."

00:01:12.327 --> 00:01:13.334
- Yeah!
(audience applauding)

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.167
(tires screeching)

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:15.690
(car crashing)
(cat shrieking)

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.987
(dramatic music)

00:01:17.987 --> 00:01:20.423
- Excuse me, sir! Ma'am, guy!

00:01:22.021 --> 00:01:23.604
Tell me your story!

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.353
Ma'am, I asked you a question!

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.337
This is "Drew's News!"

00:01:33.313 --> 00:01:34.527
This is "Drew's News."

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.459
It's "Drew's News."

00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:39.039
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:42.970
Hi, well, we're gonna get right into it

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.420
because for the first time ever,

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.350
at-home prime-time Emmys was last night,

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.415
so we got to do "About
Last Night: Emmys Edition."

00:01:52.415 --> 00:01:53.691
(Drew snaps fingers)
(audience cheering)

00:01:53.691 --> 00:01:56.772
(camera shutter clicking)
All right!

00:01:56.772 --> 00:02:00.323
Oh, I love the paparazzi sound effect.

00:02:00.323 --> 00:02:02.900
Here to help us is Emmy winner himself,

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.480
the lovable and effervescent,

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.090
even at 6:00 a.m. L.A.
time, Ross Matthews.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.810
Hello, Ross!
(audience applauding)

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:09.977
- Well, hello!

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.050
Hi!
- Oh, Ross, I love

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:17.660
when you stepped into all
of our lives with Jay Leno,

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.670
and you've really just been
someone that every time we see,

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.970
you're smart, you're funny,

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.820
we love your take on everything.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.200
You make the world a better place.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.110
- Oh, I might just wake up at 5:00 a.m.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.875
every morning for you here in L.A.

00:02:30.875 --> 00:02:31.960
if you're going to talk
like that, sweetheart.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.870
- Ross, I will always
make it worth your while.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:34.730
And have you slept?

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.893
Because you won a third Emmy last night.

00:02:36.893 --> 00:02:37.851
(audience applauding)
(Drew cheering)

00:02:37.851 --> 00:02:40.860
- "Ru Paul's Drag Race," we won again!

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.000
Let me tell you, look at
that. It is unbelievable.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.540
I love award seasons.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.780
They're like my Christmas,
my Easter, my Thanksgiving.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.760
Ever since I was a little kid,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.100
my mom bought me an old red
towel at a thrift store,

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.680
we put it on the front porch,
and I used to pose on it

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.140
and pretend I was on the red carpet.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.692
And now, Drew, look at life!

00:02:57.692 --> 00:02:58.525
It's amazing.
- I love that!

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.640
Well, illuminate us
with all of your wisdom.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.430
We have to talk about "Schitt's Creek."

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.599
I mean, they schwepped-

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:07.880
(audience chuckling)

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.240
I mean, every category.
They won everything.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.167
And just when you were
about to kinda be like,

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:15.720
"All right, spread it
out, share the love,"

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.640
the Levys would come and do these speeches

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.980
that were so gracious and incredible.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.540
You're like, "You know what?
You just take everything.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.430
You go right ahead. Have it all."

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.500
- Well, listen, people
kind of heard of the show.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.460
It got some big Emmy
nominations last year,

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.850
and I think in quarantine,

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.860
it was like the perfect show to binge.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.930
And that also happened to be

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.010
when everyone was voting on awards,

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.950
and that party, the fact
that they were all together.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.587
I kind of was so happy for
'em, but also was like,

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.530
"Can anyone get an appetizer around here?"

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.887
Every two seconds, I've got
to stand up and make a speech.

00:03:45.887 --> 00:03:48.060
(chuckling) But it really was so great

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.100
to see this little show that
could with comedy legends

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.210
winning a historic seven, all
big, all in seven categories.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:58.930
- I also think that
when it's a last season,

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.650
it's like, "We wanna celebrate
your entire board vision

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.760
of legacy that you've
left in the entire show."

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.160
So, well done.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.720
Listen, I love Ramy Youssef.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.820
He had like Jeff Spicoli attire,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.950
which is something I totally relate to.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.940
And then he put this out on social,

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.120
which I thought was hilarious.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.060
This is what happens when
you don't win the Emmy,

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:25.060
and the guy in a hazmat suit
just has to kind of walk away.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.480
- Because they were
delivering all the Emmys,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.313
just like this.

00:04:28.313 --> 00:04:30.310
Like Uber Eats, this was Uber Emmys.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.534
where they just brought it
(Drew laughing)

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.040
to their houses.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.050
But, I mean, please don't take it away.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.050
Can you just wait in the car?

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.480
If I'm not gonna win, I
don't want to see it, okay?

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.130
- It was like, this is how
you lose the Emmys in 2020.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.060
Wait, we have to talk about Zendaya,

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.640
who is just one of my favorite
people on planet Earth

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.810
for every reason in the world.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.250
And her win was history last night,

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.610
or herstory, as we're saying now.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.773
Yeah, I finally got that one.

00:04:56.773 --> 00:04:57.606
- Yeah, good for you.

00:04:57.606 --> 00:05:00.000
- And it took me a
minute to learn herstory.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.690
But she's the youngest person
ever to win lead drama.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.120
- 24 years old. She is the youngest.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.740
She's only the second
African American woman

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.650
after Viola Davis.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.020
Now, listen, the previous youngest winner,

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.380
it was Jody Comer last year, who was 26,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.213
won for "Killing Eve."

00:05:15.213 --> 00:05:16.506
- [Drew] Oh.

00:05:16.506 --> 00:05:18.610
- What I loved Zendaya's
speech is that she talked

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.740
about the young people
in the streets right now,

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.150
thanking them for keep fighting.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.760
And just looking at her with
that Emmy virtually, at home,

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.750
it was just such a 2020 moment,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.480
like such a time capsule right now.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.240
- And her, not to be shallow,

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.420
but her fashion couldn't
have been more on point.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.810
She is a walking mood board

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.440
of sort of how one can express themselves.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.020
And I just think she's so deserving

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.020
and such an inspiration
for the next generation.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.830
And then I'm just gonna end it on,

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.180
I have to go out on the
laugh, Alex Borstein.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.810
I was like, "Wait, what is going on here?

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.890
Why is she doing this?"
But I was so into it!

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.940
I'm like, "I like weird,"
and she really gave it up.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:01.773
- Let me tell you something,

00:06:01.773 --> 00:06:04.190
she is #mood for all of us right now.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.780
It's like, all I want to do
is be in like a silk robe,

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.180
and some champagne,
laying on a chaise lounge.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.000
Can I just live that life?

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.730
- I just thought, "Thank you,
you gave me some eye candy,"

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.210
and this was sort of odd,

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:18.550
and the whole thing was
very unique and interesting.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.380
And I don't know where we go from here,

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.170
but I appreciated what Jimmy Kimmel

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.470
and everybody did last night,

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:26.730
and I thank you for being here to recap

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.530
what's happening with the Emmys 2020.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.950
And congratulations, Ross!
- Thank you, my love!

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:32.783
Thank you so much.

00:06:32.783 --> 00:06:34.290
It was so great to have
the Emmy's last night.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.700
The world feels crazy, and
it felt like a little piece

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.010
of almost normal last night,

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:38.843
so thank you.
- That's why we got

00:06:38.843 --> 00:06:41.110
right into it today, so
thank you for helping us.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.720
I love you, and please come back ASAP.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.412
- I promise I will. Thank you, my love.

00:06:45.412 --> 00:06:46.440
(audience applauding)
(audience cheering)

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.832
(upbeat music)

00:06:49.832 --> 00:06:52.332
♪ Hey, oh, oh ♪

